# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts.
#
# `coverage.*` is deliberately absent. macOS matches gitignore patterns
# case-insensitively, so it swallowed test/differential/COVERAGE.md — a document
# CLAUDE.md tells a reader to consult before trusting the harness, which was
# therefore never in the repository at all. The generated artefacts are named
# explicitly instead.
*.out
coverage.html
coverage.txt
coverage.xml
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Docker Hub publication credentials for scripts/publish-docker-community.sh.
# Keep these outside the Compose .env so a registry token is never supplied to
# an application container.
.env.docker-publish

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Build and coverage output
/cover.out
/bin/

# Pinned code-generation binaries, installed by `make proto`.
.tools/

# Model artefacts fetched by scripts/fetch-model.sh. Ninety megabytes of
# weights are not a thing a source repository holds.
.models/

# The Rust reference corpora, regenerated by `make fixtures`. 22 MB of derived
# bytes that the same seed reproduces byte for byte against the frozen tree —
# the pinned digests in scripts/generate-fixtures.sh are what is worth keeping,
# not the corpora. The tests that read them skip when they are absent.
/fixtures/rust/

# rapid writes a reproduction file under testdata/rapid/ when a property test
# fails. It is a local debugging artefact keyed to one machine's run: the seed
# it holds only reproduces the failure against the same code, so committing it
# would pin a mystery nobody else can re-run. Property tests seed their own
# generators from drawn values instead, so a failure reproduces from the draws
# printed in the output.
testdata/rapid/

# Benchmark runs write real databases here, never under /tmp. Kept for
# inspection and never committed (bench/, scripts/benchmark.sh).
/.benchmark-data/
/.superpowers/

# The backoffice's Python virtual environment.
backoffice/backend/.venv/

# The backoffice frontend's dependencies and build output.
backoffice/frontend/node_modules/
backoffice/frontend/dist/
backoffice/frontend/coverage/
# Python bytecode and test caches, anywhere in the tree. Unanchored on purpose:
# these appear beside every package the interpreter touches, under
# backoffice/backend/ and under .benchmark-data/ alike, so a path-anchored
# pattern would miss the next place one turns up.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# The default Remem data directory for a Compose deployment in a checkout
# (REMEM_DATA_DIR, docker-compose.yml). It is a live Pebble database, not
# source.
/remem-data/
